<article class="env-lemma" id="07QI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07QI">Lemma <span data-tag="07QI">15.42.4</span> <span class="named">(Composition of regular maps)</span>.</a>  Let $A \to B$ and $B \to C$ be regular ring maps. If the fibre rings of $A \to C$ are Noetherian, then $A \to C$ is regular. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\mathfrak p \subset A$ be a prime. Let $\kappa (\mathfrak p) \subset k$ be a finite purely inseparable extension. We have to show that $C \otimes _ A k$ is regular. By Lemma <a href="/tag/07C1" data-tag="07C1">15.42.3</a> we may assume that $A = k$ and we reduce to proving that $C$ is regular. The assumption is that $B$ is regular and that $B \to C$ is flat with regular fibres. Then $C$ is regular by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/031E" data-tag="031E">10.112.8</a>. Some details omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>